{
  "appliance_id": "a8b0c3e2-5b6a-4c9f-8d1e-2f3a4b5c6d7e",
  "name": "IEC 61850 IED Subscriber",
  "category": "guest",
  "description": "IEC 61850 GOOSE/SV traffic subscriber (simulated IED). Listens for the configured APPID on its Ethernet port and reports unique frames, duplicates and round-trip latency to the console. The PRP transparency proof: exactly-once delivery across the redundant network, zero duplicates.",
  "vendor_name": "Arctic3D AB",
  "vendor_url": "https://arctic3d.xyz",
  "product_name": "IEC 61850 IED Subscriber",
  "registry_version": 6,
  "status": "experimental",
  "maintainer": "Arctic3D AB",
  "maintainer_email": "ceo@arctic3d.xyz",
  "usage": "IEC 61850 IED SUBSCRIBER\n==========================\n\nSimulated IED that listens for real IEC 61850 GOOSE (0x88B8) and\nSampled Values (0x88BA) traffic and reports unique frames, duplicates\nand round-trip latency on the console. Zero duplicates across a PRP\nnetwork or HSR ring proves exactly-once delivery. Attach the node to a\nRedBox SAN port.\n\nThe telnet aux console on port 5000 gives a shell.\n\nENVIRONMENT VARIABLES\n---------------------\n\nSet these per node (right-click the node, Configure, General,\nEnvironment).\n\n  IEC_MODE           (default subscriber)\n    IED personality: publisher or subscriber.\n\n  IEC_APPID          (default 0x1001)\n    APPID to listen for, hex. Must match the publisher.\n\n  IEC_ET             (default goose)\n    goose (0x88B8) or sv (0x88BA).\n\n  IEC_SVID           (default MU01)\n    SV svID to listen for (SV mode only).\n\nVERIFICATION\n------------\n\n  - Subscriber console shows total=, unique=, dupes= and latency\n    percentiles (min/p50/p95/max).\n  - dupes=0 across failover tests proves PRP/HSR transparency.\n  - In Wireshark, capture on the SAN: the publisher frames decode as\n    full GOOSE/SV protocol trees.",
  "docker": {
    "adapters": 1,
    "image": "ghcr.io/grymme/prp-sim:latest",
    "console_type": "telnet",
    "environment": "IEC_MODE=subscriber\nIEC_APPID=0x1001\nIEC_ET=goose"
  },
  "symbols": {
    "default": "symbols/iec61850-subscriber.svg"
  }
}
